  "notes": {
    "_leaflet": "Netto Marken-Discount, KW 28, valid Mo. 06.07.26 to Sa. 11.07.26 (cover). Pages are double-width spreads (842 x 1134 pt). o = the small comparison price under the big price: either labelled \"UVP x.xx\" or unlabelled (both taken as o; UVP is a manufacturer list price, not necessarily a previous Netto price). lp = Netto plus App price: price printed in purple #823b86 or white on a purple #823b86 tag (the text layer says \"Preis ohne App: x.xx\" next to some of them); the App price often has its own -X% and base price. Grid pages place the price block away from the text block, so every price-product link was confirmed by recomputing the printed base price (/kg, /l, /WL) where one exists. \"*\" marks items also orderable online, not a condition. Coupons and brand-wide rebates without a price (x % Rabatt, xFACH °Punkte) are not listed. Brands are inline in Netto names; b filled only when the name starts with a recognisable brand.",
    "1": "Lieken: comparison printed as range \"UVP 1.89 \u2013 1.99\" with \"bis zu \u201325%\"; o set to 199 (the bis-zu reference). Landliebe: 1.69 regular (\u201329%, UVP 2.39, 11.27/kg) and 1.49 on purple tag (\u201337%, 9.93/kg) = App price. Sheba/Whiskas also shows \"100 Extra°Punkte\" nearby (assignment unclear, not put in c). KNÜLLER DER WOCHE banner not tied to a product in the text layer.",
    "9": "Last row: three prices (0.55, 0.49, 0.69) for Lauchzwiebeln, Radieschen, Auberginen assigned left to right; no base prices to confirm (Bund/Stück). Unlabelled comparison prices (2.49, 1.49, 1.79) for Äpfel rot, Feldsalat, Petersilie taken as o.",
    "13": "Brand vs. Netto-brand comparison page; all four prices are Dauertiefpreis (no discount, no o). Magnum and Big Choc base prices are printed per kg although packs are in ml.",
    "15": "Geschnetzeltes 2.79 (\u201330%, 5.58/kg) and Bärchenwurst 1.19 (\u201333%, 13.22/kg) are on purple App tags. Schäufele, Puten-Hälse: price per kg (\"SPAREN pro kg\").",
